.TH KPM 8 "November 2026" "kryx-linux" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
kpm, kpm\-index \- CRUX Linux binary\-first package manager and repository indexer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kpm
.RI [ "global options" ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ args ...\& ]
.PP
.B kpm\-index
.RB [ \-\-index
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-packages
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-\-ports
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-\-base\-url
.IR url ]
.RB [ \-\-arch
.IR arch ]
.RB [ \-\-prune ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kpm
is a standalone Go package manager for standard CRUX Linux installations.
It consolidates binary package synchronization, installation, upgrades,
.B Pkgfile
source builds, search, querying, and package removal under a single
command\-line interface while remaining directly compatible with CRUX
.BR pkgutils .
.PP
.B kpm
operates directly on the standard CRUX package database
.RI ( /var/lib/pkg/db ),
honors directory\-level
.BR flock (2)
locking on
.IR /var/lib/pkg ,
commits database updates atomically using
.I .incomplete_transaction
and
.I .backup
files, evaluates
.IR /etc/pkgadd.conf
rules (including
.IR /var/lib/pkg/rejected/
handling), and invokes
.B /sbin/ldconfig
when
.I /etc/ld.so.conf
is present.
It introduces no conflicting binaries, database formats, or directory
layouts against stock
.BR pkgmk (8),
.BR pkgadd (8),
.BR pkgrm (8),
or
.BR pkginfo (8).
.PP
Package installation and system updates are strictly binary\-first against
the remote JSON repository index
.RI ( index.json ),
defaulting to the
.B kryx-linux/ports
release tag
.BR rolling\-x86_64 .
If no prebuilt binary exists in
.I index.json
for a requested package,
.B kpm install
and
.B kpm update
never trigger an automatic source build; instead, they report that no binary
is available and instruct the user to run
.BR "kpm build" .
.PP
Local CRUX ports trees (defaulting to
.IR /usr/ports )
are kept in place and parsed directly.
Build settings such as parallel jobs, compiler flags, source cache paths,
and archive compression are configured manually in
.IR /etc/kpm.ini .
.PP
.B kpm\-index
is the companion repository indexer used (typically in CI/release workflows)
to scan CRUX
.I <name>#<version>\-<release>.pkg.tar.<ext>
archives, compute SHA\-256 digests and sizes, optionally enrich entries
from a CRUX ports tree, and generate or update
.IR index.json .
.SH COMMANDS
All commands accept global options
.RB ( \-c /\-\-config ,
.BR \-r /\-\-root ,
.BR \-\-color ,
.BR \-\-no\-color )
before the subcommand name.
Each subcommand has short aliases for quick typing:
.B sy
.RB ( sync ),
.B up
.RB ( update ),
.BR in / i
.RB ( install ),
.BR bld / b
.RB ( build ),
.BR se / s
.RB ( search ),
.BR ls / l
.RB ( list ),
.BR rm / r / uninstall
.RB ( remove ),
and
.B h
.RB ( help ).
.TP
.B sync \fR[\fB\-\-ports\fR] [\fIcollection\fR ...]
Download the remote
.I index.json
from
.B [repo] index_url
and atomically save it to
.IR <cache_dir>/index.json .
When
.B \-\-ports
is supplied, also synchronize local CRUX ports collections by executing
matching drivers in
.I ports_drivers_dir
(default
.IR /etc/ports/drivers )
against collection configuration files in
.I ports_conf_dir
(default
.IR /etc/ports ),
with
.B PORTS_DIR
exported to the driver environment.
Optional
.I collection
arguments restrict port synchronization to those named collections.
.TP
.B update \fR[\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-sync\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fIpackage\fR ...]
Upgrade installed packages binary\-first.
Unless
.B \-\-no\-sync
is specified,
.I index.json
is synchronized first.
Installed packages (or only the named
.I package
arguments) are compared against the latest matching entries in
.IR index.json ;
packages whose installed version differs are downloaded, SHA\-256 verified,
and upgraded using CRUX
.BR pkgadd (8)
upgrade rules.
If an installed package has no binary in
.I index.json
but has a different version in the local ports tree,
.B kpm
prints a notice instructing the user to run
.B kpm build \fIpackage\fR
without compiling it automatically.
.TP
.B install \fR[\fB\-u\fR|\fB\-\-upgrade\fR] [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-deps\fR] \fIpackage\fR|\fIfile\fR ...
Install one or more packages strictly binary\-first.
Arguments that match the CRUX archive naming pattern
.I <name>#<version>\-<release>.pkg.tar.<ext>
and exist on disk are installed directly as local package files.
All other arguments are resolved against the locally synced
.IR index.json .
Before modifying the system,
.B kpm
verifies that every requested package (and any missing dependencies when
.B \-\-deps
is enabled) is present in
.I index.json
for the configured architecture.
If any binary is absent,
.B kpm
prints
.I no binary available for <pkg> ...; run: kpm build <pkg>
and exits with status 1 without building.
Available binaries are cached in
.IR <cache_dir>/bin/ ,
verified against their SHA\-256 digest, and installed with CRUX
.BR pkgadd (8)
conflict, rule, rollback, and
.B ldconfig
semantics.
.TP
.B build \fR[\fIoptions\fR] \fIport\fR ...
Locate each named
.I port
(either
.I name
or
.IR collection/name )
in place under
.I ports_dir
and compile it from its
.B Pkgfile
using the
.B [build]
and
.B [paths]
settings from
.IR kpm.ini .
Missing remote sources are downloaded into
.IR source_cache ,
verified against
.I .signature
and/or
.IR .md5sum ,
unpacked into
.IR <work_dir>/<name>/src ,
built via
.B bash
into
.IR <work_dir>/<name>/pkg ,
optionally stripped and manpage\-compressed, archived via
.B bsdtar \-\-format=gnutar
into
.I package_dir
as
.IR <name>#<version>\-<release>.pkg.tar.<compression> ,
and verified against
.IR .footprint .
If the target archive is already newer than the
.B Pkgfile
and all source files, the build is skipped as up to date unless
.B \-\-force
or
.B \-\-update\-footprint
is given.
.TP
.B search \fR[\fB\-\-installed\fR] [\fB\-\-ports\fR] [\fB\-\-binaries\fR] \fIquery\fR ...
Perform a case\-insensitive substring search on package names and
descriptions across the synced binary index, local ports tree, and
installed package database.
Multiple query tokens are joined with spaces.
Output is compact single\-line short form sorted alphabetically:
.RS
.PP
.nf
<name> <version> [<status>] \- <description>
.fi
.PP
where
.I <status>
is a comma\-separated combination of
.BR installed ,
.BR bin ,
and
.BR port .
.RE
.TP
.B list \fR[\fB\-\-ports\fR | \fB\-\-binaries\fR | \fB\-\-files \fItarget\fR | \fB\-\-owner \fIregex\fR | \fB\-\-diff\fR] [\fIcollection\fR ...]
Query installed packages, local ports, or binary index entries.
At most one mode flag may be supplied:
.RS
.TP
.I "(default, no flag)"
List installed packages from
.I <root>/var/lib/pkg/db
as
.I "<name> <version>"
(equivalent to
.BR "pkginfo \-i" ).
.TP
.B \-\-ports \fR[\fIcollection\fR ...]
List available ports under
.I ports_dir
as
.I <collection>/<port>
(equivalent to
.BR "ports \-l" ).
Positional
.I collection
arguments override
.B [paths] collections
for this invocation.
.TP
.B \-\-binaries
List available binary packages from synced
.I index.json
as
.IR "<pkgname> <latest>" .
.TP
.B \-\-files \fIpackage\fR|\fIarchive\fR
List files owned by an installed package or contained in a local CRUX
archive file (equivalent to
.BR "pkginfo \-l" ).
.TP
.B \-\-owner \fIregex\fR
Search all installed package file paths (prefixed with
.BR / )
against regular expression
.I regex
and print a
.I "Package  File"
table (equivalent to
.BR "pkginfo \-o" ).
.TP
.B \-\-diff
Display version differences between installed packages and available
binaries (or local ports when no binary is indexed) as a
.I "Source  Name  Available  Installed"
table.
.RE
.TP
.B remove \fIpackage\fR ...
.TQ
.B uninstall \fIpackage\fR ...
.TQ
.B rm \fIpackage\fR ...
Remove one or more installed packages using CRUX
.BR pkgrm (8)
policy.
Requires root privileges, acquires an exclusive lock on
.IR <root>/var/lib/pkg ,
preserves files still referenced by any other installed package, removes
remaining files and empty directories in reverse lexicographical order,
runs
.B /sbin/ldconfig \-r \fI<root>\fR
if
.I <root>/etc/ld.so.conf
exists, and commits the updated database atomically.
.TP
.B help
Print usage summary and exit 0.
.TP
.B version
Print the
.B kpm
version string and exit 0.
.SH KPM\-INDEX
.B kpm\-index
builds or updates the JSON binary repository index consumed by
.B kpm sync
and
.BR "kpm install" .
It scans
.I \-\-packages
for all CRUX archives matching
.I "*.pkg.tar.{gz,bz2,xz,lz,zst}"
whose filenames follow
.IR "<name>#<version>\-<release>.pkg.tar.<ext>" .
Unrecognized archive names produce a warning on standard error and are skipped.
.PP
For each valid archive,
.B kpm\-index
computes its SHA\-256 checksum and byte size, constructs its download URL
from
.I \-\-base\-url
using URL path escaping (encoding
.B #
as
.B %23
so archive URLs are never truncated as URL fragments), optionally enriches
.BR description ,
.BR depends ,
and
.B collection
from
.IR \-\-ports ,
merges the entry into any existing
.IR index.json ,
sorts versions ascending using numeric\-aware segment comparison, updates
each package's
.B latest
pointer, and writes the resulting JSON atomically.
.SS Index JSON Schema
.RS
.nf
{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "packages": {
    "zlib": {
      "latest": "1.3.1\-1",
      "versions": [
        {
          "pkgname": "zlib",
          "pkgver": "1.3.1",
          "pkgrel": "1",
          "arch": "x86_64",
          "filename": "zlib#1.3.1\-1.pkg.tar.zst",
          "url": "https://github.com/kryx-linux/ports/releases/download/rolling\-x86_64/zlib%231.3.1\-1.pkg.tar.zst",
          "sha256": "<hex\-sha256>",
          "size": 123456,
          "description": "Compression library",
          "depends": ["glibc"],
          "collection": "core"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
The fields
.BR description ,
.BR depends ,
and
.B collection
are omitted when empty.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Global Options (kpm)
Global options must precede the subcommand name.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIfile\fR"
Use
.I file
as the INI configuration file instead of
.I $KPM_CONFIG
or
.IR /etc/kpm.ini .
When specified explicitly, a missing file causes an error.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-root " \fIpath\fR"
Override
.B [paths] root
to operate on an alternative CRUX installation root (e.g., a mounted
chroot or staging root).
.TP
.BR \-\-color " \fImode\fR"
Control ANSI color output:
.B auto
(enable on interactive terminals unless
.B NO_COLOR
is set or
.BR TERM=dumb ),
.BR always ,
or
.B never
(default:
.B [ui] color
or
.BR auto ).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI color output (equivalent to
.BR \-\-color=never ).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit 0.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage summary and exit 0.
.SS sync Options
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-ports
In addition to downloading
.IR index.json ,
run CRUX port collection sync drivers in
.IR ports_drivers_dir .
.SS update Options
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Overwrite conflicting files during binary upgrades (still honoring
.B UPGRADE ... NO
rules from
.IR pkgadd.conf ).
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-sync
Use the already cached
.I index.json
without fetching the remote index first.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print available binary upgrades without downloading or modifying the system.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
List all conflicting files without truncation on conflict errors.
.SS install Options
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-upgrade
Upgrade an already installed package.
Required if the package is already present in
.IR /var/lib/pkg/db
(unless
.B \-\-reinstall
is used); rejected if the package is not yet installed.
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-reins ", " \-\-reinstall
Reinstall package(s) even if already installed (upgrades in place when
present, or performs a fresh install if absent).
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Remove and overwrite conflicting files owned by other packages or already
present on disk.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-deps
Recursively resolve dependencies (from
.I index.json
.B depends
or local
.B Pkgfile
headers), skip dependencies already installed, and install missing
dependencies first from
.IR index.json .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
List every conflicting file path on conflict errors instead of truncating
output after the first 20 files.
.PP
Subcommand options may appear either before or after positional arguments
(for example,
.B kpm install zig \-\-force
and
.B kpm install \-\-force zig
are equivalent); pass
.B \-\-
to end option parsing.
.SS build Options
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-install
Install each built target package after building (automatically upgrades
if the package is already installed in the database).
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-upgrade
Upgrade each built target package after building (requires the package to
be previously installed).
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-reins ", " \-\-reinstall
Force rebuilding the target port(s) and reinstall them into
.I root
whether previously installed or not.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Force rebuilding target ports even if the target archive is up to date,
and pass
.B \-\-force
when installing.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-deps
Resolve recursive
.B Pkgfile
runtime
.RB ( "# Depends on:" )
and build\-only
.RB ( "# Make depends on:" )
dependencies in topological order.
Already\-installed dependencies are skipped.
Uninstalled dependencies are installed into
.I root
before building downstream ports (using prebuilt binaries from synced
.I index.json
when available unless
.B \-\-source\-deps
is set, in which case only their runtime dependencies are needed; otherwise
building them from
.I ports_dir
and installing the resulting archive).
Binary\-only dependencies present in
.I index.json
are supported even when absent from the local ports tree.
Requested target ports are always built from source and only installed
when
.BR \-i / \-\-install ,
.BR \-u / \-\-upgrade ,
or
.BR \-R / \-\-reinstall
is passed.
.TP
.B \-\-sync
With
.BR \-d / \-\-deps ,
synchronize the remote binary
.I index.json
before resolving binary dependencies.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-source\-deps
With
.BR \-d / \-\-deps ,
always build missing dependencies from
.I ports_dir
instead of reusing prebuilt binaries from
.IR index.json .
.TP
.BR \-if ", " \-\-ignore\-footprint
Skip
.I .footprint
verification after creating the archive.
.TP
.BR \-in ", " \-\-ignore\-new
Allow
.B NEW
files during
.I .footprint
verification while still failing on
.B MISSING
files.
.TP
.BR \-uf ", " \-\-update\-footprint
Regenerate and overwrite
.I .footprint
in the port directory from the built archive.
.TP
.BR \-im ", " \-\-ignore\-md5sum
Skip
.I .md5sum
verification of source files.
.TP
.BR \-is ", " \-\-ignore\-signature
Skip
.I .signature
cryptographic verification.
.TP
.BR \-kw ", " \-\-keep\-work
Keep
.I <work_dir>/<name>
after the build completes or fails.
.TP
.BR \-ns ", " \-\-no\-strip
Disable ELF binary, shared library, and archive stripping.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
List all conflicting files without truncation when installing packages.
.SS search Options
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-installed
Search only packages installed in
.IR <root>/var/lib/pkg/db .
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-ports
Search only ports in
.IR ports_dir .
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-binaries
Search only packages in synced
.IR index.json .
.SS list Options
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-ports
List ports under
.I ports_dir
in
.I <collection>/<port>
format.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-binaries
List available binary packages from synced
.IR index.json .
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-files " \fIpackage\fR|\fIarchive\fR"
List files belonging to an installed package or a local archive file.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-owner " \fIregex\fR"
List installed packages owning files matching regular expression
.IR regex .
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-diff
List version differences between installed packages and binary/port sources.
.SS kpm\-index Options
.TP
.B \-\-index \fIpath\fR
Path to the JSON index file to create or update (default:
.IR index.json ).
.TP
.B \-\-packages \fIdir\fR
Directory containing CRUX
.I .pkg.tar.<ext>
archives to index (default:
.IR . ).
.TP
.B \-\-ports\-dir \fIdir\fR, \-\-ports \fIdir\fR
Optional CRUX ports directory used to populate
.BR description ,
.BR depends ,
.BR makedepends ,
and
.B collection
fields on indexed entries (default:
.I $KRYX_PORTS_DIR
or
.IR $KPM_PORTS_DIR ).
.TP
.B \-\-base\-url \fIurl\fR
Optional
.B http://
or
.B https://
base URL prepended to percent\-encoded archive filenames (default: empty,
storing bare filenames in
.BR url ).
.TP
.B \-\-arch \fIarch\fR
Target architecture string recorded in entries (default:
.B x86_64
on amd64 hosts, otherwise the Go architecture name).
.TP
.B \-\-prune
Remove existing index entries whose archive filename is no longer present in
.I \-\-packages
(default:
.BR false ).
.TP
.B \-\-sign\-key \fIprivkey\fR
Generate an OpenBSD
.BR signify (1)\-compatible
detached signature
.RI ( <index>.sig )
using a signify
.I .sec
or
.B kryx\-ed25519
private key.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B kpm
reads a manual INI configuration file (default
.IR /etc/kpm.ini ).
If no explicit config file is requested via
.B \-\-config
or
.B KPM_CONFIG
and
.I /etc/kpm.ini
does not exist, built\-in defaults are used.
Lines beginning with
.B #
or
.B ;
are comments; inline comments preceded by whitespace are also stripped.
Values may be enclosed in single or double quotes.
Boolean keys accept
.BR true / yes / 1 / on
and
.BR false / no / 0 / off .
List keys accept comma\- or whitespace\-separated items.
.SS [paths]
Keys in
.B [paths]
are also accepted before any section header.
.TP
.B root
CRUX installation root directory (default:
.IR / ).
.TP
.B ports_dir
Local CRUX ports tree path, used in place (default:
.IR /usr/ports ).
.TP
.B collections
Priority\-ordered list of port collections under
.I ports_dir
(default:
.BR "core, opt, xorg, contrib" ).
Leave empty to auto\-discover all collections.
.TP
.B cache_dir
Base cache directory for
.I index.json
and downloaded binaries under
.I bin/
(default:
.IR /var/cache/kpm ).
.TP
.B source_cache \fR(alias: \fBsource_dir\fR)
Cache directory for downloaded upstream source files used by
.B kpm build
(default:
.IR /var/cache/kpm/sources ).
.TP
.B package_dir
Output directory where
.B kpm build
writes compiled
.I .pkg.tar.<ext>
archives (default:
.IR /var/cache/kpm/packages ).
.TP
.B work_dir
Temporary build work directory containing
.I <name>/src
and
.I <name>/pkg
(default:
.IR /var/cache/kpm/work ).
.TP
.B pkgadd_conf
Path to CRUX
.BR pkgadd.conf (8)
rule file (default:
.IR /etc/pkgadd.conf ).
If absent, the implicit default rule installs and upgrades all files.
.TP
.B ports_conf_dir
Directory containing CRUX port collection config files for
.B kpm sync \-\-ports
(default:
.IR /etc/ports ).
.TP
.B ports_drivers_dir
Directory containing executable CRUX port sync drivers (default:
.IR /etc/ports/drivers ).
.SS [repo]
.TP
.B repository
GitHub repository slug hosting binary releases (default:
.BR kryx-linux/ports ).
.TP
.B tag
Release tag containing
.I index.json
and binary assets (default:
.BR rolling\-x86_64 ).
.TP
.B arch
Target architecture selected from
.I index.json
(default:
.BR x86_64 ;
entries with
.B arch
empty or
.B any
also match).
.TP
.B index_url
Full
.B http://
or
.B https://
URL to
.IR index.json .
If omitted while
.B repository
and
.B tag
are set, it is derived automatically from those values.
Default:
.RS
.nf
https://github.com/kryx-linux/ports/releases/download/rolling\-x86_64/index.json
.fi
.RE
.TP
.B timeout_seconds
HTTP timeout in seconds for syncing
.I index.json
and downloading binaries or sources (default:
.BR 120 ,
minimum
.BR 1 ).
.SS [build]
.TP
.B jobs
Parallel build jobs exported as
.B JOBS
(default: host CPU count;
.I kpm.ini.example
sets
.BR 4 ).
.TP
.B cflags
C compiler flags exported as
.B CFLAGS
(default:
.BR "\-O2 \-march=x86\-64 \-pipe" ).
.TP
.B cxxflags
C++ compiler flags exported as
.B CXXFLAGS
(defaults to the value of
.B cflags
if unset).
.TP
.B ldflags
Linker flags exported as
.B LDFLAGS
when non\-empty (default: empty).
.TP
.B makeflags
Flags exported as
.B MAKEFLAGS
(defaults to
.BI \-j <jobs>
if unset).
.TP
.B compression
Archive compression mode for
.B kpm build
(default:
.BR zst ).
Supported values are
.BR gz ,
.BR bz2 ,
.BR xz ,
.BR lz ,
and
.BR zst .
.TP
.B source_mirrors
Optional space\- or comma\-separated mirror base URLs tried before upstream
source URLs (default: empty).
.TP
.B download_sources
Download missing remote sources into
.I source_cache
(default:
.BR true ).
.TP
.B strip
Strip unstripped ELF executables, shared objects, and static archives in
.I $PKG
while honoring
.I .nostrip
(default:
.BR true ).
.TP
.B compress_manpages
Compress man pages under
.I */man/man*/*
with
.B gzip \-9
and update man page symlinks (default:
.BR true ).
.TP
.B ignore_footprint
Skip
.I .footprint
verification (default:
.BR false ).
.TP
.B ignore_new
Permit
.B NEW
files during
.I .footprint
verification (default:
.BR false ).
.TP
.B ignore_md5sum
Skip
.I .md5sum
verification (default:
.BR false ).
.TP
.B ignore_signature
Skip
.I .signature
verification via
.B signify
(default:
.BR true ).
.TP
.B keep_work
Preserve
.I <work_dir>/<name>
after builds (default:
.BR false ).
.TP
.B download_prog
Fallback downloader program for non\-HTTP(S) schemes such as
.B ftp://
.RB ( curl
or
.BR wget ;
default:
.BR curl ).
.TP
.B curl_opts\fR, \fBwget_opts
Extra options appended when invoking
.B curl
or
.B wget
(default: empty).
.SS [ui]
.TP
.B color
Default ANSI color mode:
.BR auto ,
.BR always ,
or
.B never
(default:
.BR auto ).
.SS pkgadd.conf Rules
.B kpm
parses
.I /etc/pkgadd.conf
(or the path configured in
.BR "[paths] pkgadd_conf" )
using the exact three\-column CRUX format:
.RS
.PP
.nf
<EVENT> <REGEX> <YES|NO>
.fi
.RE
.PP
where
.I EVENT
is
.B INSTALL
or
.B UPGRADE
and the last matching rule takes precedence.
Files excluded by
.B INSTALL ... NO
are omitted from both extraction and the package database.
Existing files matched by
.B UPGRADE ... NO
are preserved on disk and the incoming version is extracted under
.IR <root>/var/lib/pkg/rejected/ ;
if the rejected file has identical permissions and identical or empty
contents, it is automatically pruned from
.IR rejected/ .
.SH PKGFILE FORMAT
.B kpm build
and
.B kpm search
parse standard CRUX
.B Pkgfile
recipes directly from the local ports tree.
.SS Header Comments
Leading
.B #
comment lines are parsed for metadata:
.TP
.B # Description: \fItext\fR
Short one\-line package summary used by
.B kpm search
and
.BR "kpm\-index \-\-ports" .
.TP
.B # URL: \fIurl\fR
Upstream project homepage.
.TP
.B # Maintainer: \fIcontact\fR
Port maintainer information.
.TP
.B # Packager: \fIcontact\fR
Original packager information.
.TP
.B # Depends on: \fIpkg1 pkg2\fR ... \fR(also accepts \fB# Depends:\fR)
Space\- or comma\-separated list of runtime dependencies used by
.BR "kpm build \-\-deps" ,
.BR "kpm install \-\-deps" ,
and
.BR "kpm\-index \-\-ports" .
.TP
.B # Make depends on: \fIpkg1 pkg2\fR ... \fR(also accepts \fB# Make depends:\fR, \fB# Makedepends:\fR, \fB# Build depends on:\fR)
Optional, fully backward\-compatible header listing build\-time\-only dependencies
(such as compilers or code generators).
Satisfied during
.B kpm build \-\-deps
and
.B kryx\-src pkg \-\-deps
(binary\-first from
.I index.json
when available, otherwise built from source), and recorded separately from runtime
.B depends
so
.B kpm install \-\-deps
does not pull build\-only tools onto end\-user systems.
Ports omitting this header continue to work identically to stock CRUX.
.SS Required and Optional Shell Definitions
.B Pkgfile
recipes are evaluated in
.B bash
with
.BR LC_ALL=C.UTF\-8 :
.TP
.BR name ", " version ", " release
Mandatory shell variables identifying the package name, upstream version,
and CRUX release number.
.TP
.B source=(\fIentry\fR ...)
Optional bash array of source files.
Entries beginning with
.BR http:// ,
.BR https:// ,
.BR ftp:// ,
or
.B file://
are fetched into
.IR source_cache ;
all other entries are resolved as local files in the port directory.
.TP
.B renames=(\fIname\fR|SKIP ...)
Optional bash array parallel to
.BR source ,
renaming downloaded files inside
.IR source_cache .
Use
.B SKIP
to leave an entry unrenamed.
.TP
.B build()
Mandatory bash function executed with
.B set \-e
and
.B umask 022
in working directory
.IR $SRC ,
installing package files into
.IR $PKG .
.TP
.B unpack_source()
Optional bash function overriding the default source extraction step
(which extracts tar/zip/rpm/7z archives with
.B bsdtar \-p \-o \-C "$SRC" \-xf
and copies non\-archive files into
.IR $SRC ).
.SS Companion Port Files and Output Archive
Integrity and packaging checks follow CRUX
.BR pkgmk (8)
conventions using companion files in the port directory rather than in\-file
checksum arrays:
.TP
.I .md5sum
MD5 digests of source files checked before
.B build()
unless ignored.
.TP
.I .signature
Cryptographic
.B signify
signature covering
.BR Pkgfile ,
.IR .footprint ,
and source files, verified when
.B ignore_signature = false
and
.B \-\-ignore\-signature
is not set.
.TP
.I .footprint
Expected sorted package file listing (normalizing
.I lib/modules/<uname \-r>/
to
.IR lib/modules/<kernel\-version>/ ).
If absent on first build,
.B kpm build
warns and creates a new
.IR .footprint .
.TP
.I .nostrip
Line\-delimited patterns passed to
.B grep \-v \-f
to exclude files from ELF stripping.
.PP
Built archives are written to
.I <package_dir>/<name>#<version>\-<release>.pkg.tar.<compression>
using
.B bsdtar \-\-format=gnutar
(falling back to
.B tar
if
.B bsdtar
is absent).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KPM_CONFIG
Path to the INI configuration file used when
.BR \-c / \-\-config
is not passed on the command line.
Setting
.B KPM_CONFIG
treats the configuration path as explicit (failing if the file cannot be read).
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set to any non\-empty value, disables ANSI color output in
.B auto
color mode.
.TP
.B TERM
When set to
.BR dumb ,
disables ANSI color output in
.B auto
color mode.
.TP
.B PATH
Searched for helper utilities used during archive handling, builds, and
verification:
.BR bash ,
.BR bsdtar ,
.BR tar ,
.BR xz ,
.BR zstd ,
.BR lzip ,
.BR gzip ,
.BR strip ,
.BR file ,
.BR signify ,
.BR curl ,
.BR wget ,
and
.BR uname .
.SS Exported to Child Processes
During
.B kpm sync \-\-ports
the variable
.B PORTS_DIR
is exported to each port driver.
During
.B kpm build
the following variables are exported to the
.B Pkgfile
shell:
.BR SRC ,
.BR PKG ,
.BR PKGMK_ROOT ,
.BR PKGMK_SOURCE_DIR ,
.BR PKGMK_PACKAGE_DIR ,
.BR PKGMK_WORK_DIR ,
.BR JOBS ,
.BR CFLAGS ,
.BR CXXFLAGS ,
.BR LDFLAGS
(when configured),
.BR MAKEFLAGS ,
and
.BR LC_ALL=C.UTF\-8 .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/kpm.ini
Default manual INI configuration file.
.TP
.I /etc/pkgadd.conf
CRUX
.B INSTALL
and
.B UPGRADE
file handling rules.
.TP
.I /etc/ld.so.conf
Checked under
.I <root>
before executing
.B /sbin/ldconfig \-r \fI<root>\fR.
.TP
.IR /etc/ports/ ", " /etc/ports/drivers/
CRUX port collection definitions and executable drivers invoked by
.BR "kpm sync \-\-ports" .
.TP
.I /usr/ports
Default local CRUX ports tree.
.TP
.I <root>/var/lib/pkg
Directory locked via non\-blocking
.BR flock (2)
.RB ( LOCK_SH
for read\-only commands,
.B LOCK_EX
for install, upgrade, and remove transactions).
.TP
.I <root>/var/lib/pkg/db
CRUX plain\-text installed package database.
.TP
.I <root>/var/lib/pkg/db.incomplete_transaction
Temporary mode\-0444 staging file synchronized with
.BR fsync (2)
before atomic database replacement.
.TP
.I <root>/var/lib/pkg/db.backup
Hardlink backup of the previous database created immediately prior to
renaming the committed transaction into place.
.TP
.I <root>/var/lib/pkg/rejected/
Directory storing upgraded files held back by
.B UPGRADE ... NO
rules when their content or permissions differ from the installed version.
.TP
.I /var/lib/kpm/world
Explicitly installed package list (locked alongside
.IR /var/lib/pkg )
used by
.B kpm info
and
.BR "kpm autoremove" .
.TP
.I /var/lib/kpm/hold
Pinned/held packages skipped during
.B kpm update
(merged with
.B [repo] hold
in
.IR /etc/kpm.ini ).
.TP
.I /var/cache/kpm/index.json
Locally cached binary repository index written by
.BR "kpm sync" .
.TP
.I /var/cache/kpm/bin/
Cache directory for downloaded, SHA\-256 verified binary archives.
.TP
.I /var/cache/kpm/sources/
Cache directory for downloaded upstream source archives used by
.BR "kpm build" .
.TP
.I /var/cache/kpm/packages/
Default output directory for archives built with
.BR "kpm build" .
.TP
.I /var/cache/kpm/work/
Temporary build directory containing per\-port
.I src/
and
.I pkg/
subdirectories.
.SH ADVANCED COMMANDS
.TP
.B kpm info \fIpkg\fR ...
Display full metadata (Name, Version, Collection, Description, URL, Installed status, Runtime Depends, Make Depends, and Required By reverse dependencies).
.TP
.B kpm autoremove \fR[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
Identify and remove orphaned dependency packages no longer required by any package listed in
.IR /var/lib/kpm/world .
.TP
.B kpm clean \fR[\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-bin\fR] [\fB\-\-sources\fR] [\fB\-\-packages\fR] [\fB\-\-keep \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
Prune stale cached binary archives, partial downloads, locally built packages, and unused upstream sources while retaining installed/latest
.I N
versions by default.
.TP
.B kpm check \fR[\fB\-\-broken\fR] [\fB\-\-files\fR] [\fIpkg\fR ...]
With
.BR \-\-broken ,
scans installed ELF binaries and shared libraries natively in Go (equivalent to CRUX
.BR revdep )
to report missing
.I .so
shared library dependencies and affected packages.
With
.BR \-\-files ,
verifies every file recorded in
.I /var/lib/pkg/db
exists on disk with expected types and permissions.
Without flags, runs
.BR "kpm doctor" .
.TP
.B kpm hold \fR[\fB\-\-list\fR | \fIpkg\fR ...] / \fBkpm unhold \fIpkg\fR ...
Pin or unpin packages in
.I /var/lib/kpm/hold
(also configurable via
.B [repo] hold = pkg1, pkg2
in
.IR /etc/kpm.ini ).
Held packages are skipped by
.B kpm update
unless
.B \-\-ignore\-hold
is passed.
.TP
.B kpm install \fIpkg\fB=\fIver\fR / \fBkpm downgrade \fIpkg\fR[\fB=\fIver\fR]
Install a specific package version from
.I index.json
or
.IR /var/cache/kpm/bin/ ,
or roll back an installed package to its previous available version.
.TP
.B kpm rejected \fR[\fB\-\-list\fR | \fB\-\-diff\fR | \fB\-\-keep \fIfile|all\fR | \fB\-\-upgrade \fIfile|all\fR | \fB\-\-merge \fIfile|all\fR]
Inspect, diff, keep, upgrade, or conflict\-merge files in
.I /var/lib/pkg/rejected/
(non\-interactively or interactively via the shared
.BR rejmerge (8)
backend).
.SH CRUX MULTI\-CALL SYMLINK COMPATIBILITY
When
.B kpm
is invoked via compatibility symlinks installed in
.I /usr/bin
(created by default via
.BR "make install" ),
it dispatches on
.B argv[0]
with 100% upstream CRUX flag, configuration, output, and exit\-code parity:
.TP
.B pkgadd
Supports
.BR \-u / \-\-upgrade ,
.BR \-f / \-\-force ,
.BR \-r / \-\-root ,
.BR \-c / \-\-config ,
.BR \-v ,
.BR \-h ,
and exact
.I /etc/pkgadd.conf
+
.I /var/lib/pkg/rejected/
semantics.
.TP
.B pkgrm
Supports
.BR \-r / \-\-root ,
.BR \-v ,
.BR \-h ,
shared\-file preservation, and reverse directory cleanup.
.TP
.B pkginfo
Supports
.BR \-i / \-\-installed ,
.BR \-l / \-\-list ,
.BR \-o / \-\-owner ,
.BR \-f / \-\-footprint
(archives and directories),
.BR \-r / \-\-root ,
.BR \-v ,
.BR \-h
with exact stock CRUX output formatting.
.TP
.B pkgmk
Supports all 26 upstream flags
.RB ( \-i ,
.BR \-u ,
.BR \-r ,
.BR \-d ,
.BR \-do ,
.BR \-eo ,
.BR \-utd ,
.BR \-uf ,
.BR \-if ,
.BR \-in ,
.BR \-um ,
.BR \-im ,
.BR \-cm ,
.BR \-us ,
.BR \-cs ,
.BR \-is ,
.BR \-rs ,
.BR \-sk ,
.BR \-pk ,
.BR \-ns ,
.BR \-f ,
.BR \-c ,
.BR \-kw ,
.BR \-cf ,
.BR \-v ,
.BR \-h ),
.I /etc/pkgmk.conf
and
.B PKGMK_*
environment variables,
.I .32bit
architecture detection, current\-directory
.B Pkgfile
execution with no arguments, and upstream exit codes
.BR 1 .. 10 .
.TP
.B ports
Supports
.BR \-u / \-\-update " [collection...],"
.BR \-l / \-\-list ,
.BR \-d / \-\-diff ,
.BR \-v ,
.BR \-h ,
and custom drivers in
.IR /etc/ports/drivers/ .
.TP
.B rejmerge
Supports
.BR \-r / \-\-root ,
.BR \-v ,
.BR \-h ,
interactive permissions/diff/merge/file menus, and automatic empty directory cleanup.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.SS kpm
.TP
.B 0
Command completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Operational error (configuration load error, missing binary in
.IR index.json ,
HTTP, signature, or SHA\-256 verification failure, database lock contention, file
conflict without
.BR \-\-force ,
reverse dependency refusal without
.BR \-\-force ,
build or footprint failure, or missing root privileges for package
installation/removal).
.TP
.B 2
Command\-line usage error (missing subcommand, unknown global option, or
unknown subcommand).
.SS kpm\-index
.TP
.B 0
Repository index created or updated successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Operational error (invalid
.BR \-\-base\-url ,
unreadable existing index, signing error, or filesystem write failure).
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command\-line flag syntax.
.SH EXAMPLES
Synchronize the remote binary index (with optional signature verification) and CRUX ports collections:
.RS
.PP
.nf
kpm sync
kpm sync \-\-verify
kpm sync \-\-ports core opt
.fi
.RE
.PP
Search across binaries, local ports, and installed packages, inspect full metadata, and list ports/installed packages:
.RS
.PP
.nf
kpm search zlib
kpm info zlib
kpm list \-\-ports
kpm list \-\-diff
kpm list \-\-owner 'usr/bin/git$'
.fi
.RE
.PP
Install a binary package (or a pinned version) with its binary dependencies:
.RS
.PP
.nf
kpm install \-\-deps git
kpm install zlib=1.3.1\-1
.fi
.RE
.PP
When no binary exists in
.IR index.json ,
explicitly build and install the port from the local CRUX ports tree:
.RS
.PP
.nf
kpm build \-\-deps \-\-install myport
.fi
.RE
.PP
Preview and apply binary\-first system upgrades, hold/unhold, downgrade, prune orphans, clean cache, and check ABI/file health:
.RS
.PP
.nf
kpm update \-\-dry\-run
kpm update
kpm hold linux
kpm downgrade foo
kpm remove myport
kpm autoremove \-\-dry\-run
kpm clean \-\-keep 2
kpm check \-\-broken
kpm check \-\-files
kpm rejected \-\-list
.fi
.RE
.PP
Install a package into an alternative CRUX root filesystem using a custom
INI configuration:
.RS
.PP
.nf
kpm \-\-config /etc/kpm.ini \-\-root /mnt/crux install zlib
.fi
.RE
.PP
Generate, prune, and sign
.I index.json
for a
.B rolling\-x86_64
release using
.BR kpm\-index :
.RS
.PP
.nf
kpm\-index \e
  \-\-packages ./pkg \e
  \-\-ports\-dir /usr/ports \e
  \-\-index ./pkg/index.json \e
  \-\-arch x86_64 \e
  \-\-base\-url https://github.com/kryx-linux/ports/releases/download/rolling\-x86_64 \e
  \-\-sign\-key ./kryx\-release.sec \e
  \-\-prune
.fi
.RE
